meta {
  name: Update Radiology Panel
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/radiology-panels/{{radiologyPanelId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "panelName": "CT Chest + Abdomen Combo (2026)",
    "priceMsrp": 9500,
    "priceMaximum": 9000,
    "priceMinimum": 6500,
    "turnaroundPriority": "URGENT",
    "isPreference": true,
    "panelInstructions": "Fast for 6 hours before the contrast study",
    "tests": [
      {
        "radiologyTestId": "{{radiologyTestId}}",
        "sortOrder": 1,
        "isRemovable": true,
        "discountPercent": 5
      }
    ]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 2db13b5e-4a25-412f-bcd9-68bcbeea9d59
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires **any of** `business_admin:master_data__update_lab_panel`
  OR `business_admin:master_data__edit_the_panel` (`@RequireAnyPermission`) —
  enforced by `PermissionGuard`; admins bypass, so `{{businessAccessToken}}`
  succeeds. (Reuses the master-data lab-panel permission keys.)

  Update a radiology panel's scalar fields. Business JWT. Partial update (explicit
  optionals, not `PartialType`) — send only what changes. Same field set and enums
  as "Create Radiology Panel" (all optional here).

  **When `tests` is provided the whole member-test set is REPLACED** — the old
  active rows are soft-deleted and the supplied set is created. Omit `tests` to
  leave the composition untouched. Each supplied `radiologyTestId` must reference an
  active RadiologyTest in the same master data (404 `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_TEST_NOT_FOUND`
  otherwise) and `discountPercent` is re-checked against that test's `discountCapPct`.

  Conflicts: 409 `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_NAME_CONFLICT` / `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_CODE_CONFLICT`
  (unique per master data among active rows). 404 `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_NOT_FOUND` /
  `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
}
